// Jahshaka's DDGI diffuse INTENSITY — the one thing upstream's IrradianceField
// has no knob for (GI_UNIFIED_SPEC.md §4 P1 / addendum item 2).
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Binding an IrradianceField makes HlmsPbs set
// `VctDisableDiffuse` (OgreHlmsPbs.cpp:1784-1788): DDGI does not ADD to voxel
// cone tracing's diffuse, it REPLACES it — and the P0 spike measured the
// replacement at ~13x dimmer than the (over-bright, leak-prone) VCT diffuse it
// takes over from. Every scene therefore gets markedly darker the moment the
// field binds, and `IrradianceFieldSettings` carries nothing to scale it with.
// So the scalar is OURS, applied at the last line of upstream's own piece, and
// it rides the pass buffer (a const-buffer write, never a shader rebuild) so
// the author can turn the dial without a recompile.
//
// WHY A WHOLE-PIECE COPY RATHER THAN A HOOK. There is no hook: the insert order
// is `applyVoxelConeTracing` -> `applyIrradianceField` -> `forwardPlusDoCubemaps`
// (Hlms/Pbs/Any/Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any:911-913), and the field's
// contribution is accumulated into `pixelData.envColourD` inside the piece's
// last statement. Anything that ran later would scale the probe/cubemap terms
// too. The Hlms parser rejects a duplicate piece NAME, so the pattern is the one
// JahFog_piece_vs_piece_ps.any already uses for `DoAtmosphereNprSky`: UNDEF the
// piece, then define it again — from a library folder that is loaded LAST
// (OgreEngine::ensureHlms appends Hlms/Jahshaka after upstream's Pbs paths, so
// the original has been collected by the time this file is parsed).
//
// THE BODY IS UPSTREAM'S, VERBATIM, save the final multiply. It is duplicated
// code and that is a maintenance cost we pay deliberately, guarded rather than
// trusted: irisgl/engine/CMakeLists.txt hashes
// Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/IrradianceField_piece_ps.any at configure time and
// FAILS the configure when upstream's body changes, so a pin bump cannot leave
// this copy silently stale (re-sync the body, re-apply the multiply, update the
// hash). No Ogre patch is involved anywhere in this route.
//
// CAUTION, the same one JahFog and JahVct carry, and this file cost the lane a
// full test run by ignoring it: the Hlms parser does NOT respect // comments —
// an at-directive written inside a comment is EXECUTED, and a stray parenthesis
// after one is a syntax error that silently drops every definition in the file
// (the shader still compiles; it just uses upstream's piece, so the symptom is
// "my override does nothing"). Every directive is therefore named in WORDS
// above, never written with its at-sign.
//
// THE SECOND THING THAT IS NOT UPSTREAM'S: THE AMBIENT SKY-VISIBILITY TERM
// (the Rayon ambient fix; GI_UNIFIED_SPEC.md ADDENDUM CORRECTION, and the
// ledger entries "Vct_piece_ps.any: volume-local ambient blend commented out"
// and "IrradianceField nits" in SPECS/OGRE_UPSTREAM_ISSUES.md).
//
// THE GAP. Inside a VCT volume the PBS ambient term is dead: every ambient
// piece is wrapped in `if( vctSpecular.w == 0 )` and upstream commented the
// volume-local blend out, hardcoding blend = 1.0, so vctSpecular.w is never
// zero and DoAmbientLighting can never fire while VctLighting is bound. The
// only live ambient in a VCT scene was the cone-traced diffuse's own
// `light.xyz += ambient * light.w` — ambient times the ESCAPE FRACTION of its
// cones, i.e. ambient weighted by how much sky the surface can see. Binding an
// irradiance field sets VctDisableDiffuse, which deletes that whole branch, and
// the field's own generation job computes the same escape fraction and THROWS
// IT AWAY (IrradianceFieldGenFromVct_piece_cs.any: `alpha` is local to
// voxelConeTraceDiff and never returned). So with DDGI on, ambient light inside
// the volume comes from nowhere: measured as a 15-25% darker mid-ground on open
// scenes, and correctly zero in sealed rooms, which is why it reads as "flat"
// rather than as "broken".
//
// THE PROXY, and why it is a proxy. We cannot recover the cones' escape
// fraction (it is thrown away inside a compute job we do not patch), but the
// field's DEPTH atlas already answers the same question: it stores, per probe
// and per octahedral direction, how far the generation rays travelled, in
// probe-grid units. A ray that hit nothing exits the march at the loop's own
// limit (`while( dist < 1.414213562f && alpha < 0.95 )`) and its stored
// distance is `1.414213562 * dot( abs( dir ), numProbes )` — the exact
// expression the job uses to convert march distance into the units the pixel
// shader compares against. Anything shorter means the ray hit geometry.
//
// WHAT A DEPTH TEXEL ACTUALLY HOLDS — corrected 2026-09-09 (rayon2 S1), and
// the correction is the whole design. The first version of this file claimed
// a texel was ONE ray at our settings (depthRes 12, raysPerPixel 1). It is
// not: upstream's generation workspace runs `IrradianceField/Integration/Depth`
// after every generation dispatch (IrradianceField.compositor), and that job
// convolves the depth atlas with a COSINE LOBE over the whole hemisphere —
// `fillIntegrationWeights` weights every texel whose direction has a positive
// dot with the texel being written, normalised (OgreIrradianceField.cpp:365).
// Both channels get it. So a depth texel is the cosine-weighted MEAN distance
// over the hemisphere around its direction, and the second channel is the
// cosine-weighted mean of the SQUARED distances. That single fact explains the
// old single-tap defect exactly: comparing a hemisphere mean against the
// escape distance of the ONE direction at its centre. On an anisotropic probe
// grid (32x8x32 is the shape our fit gives a room) the escape distance of the
// rays tilted toward the dense axes is up to four times the straight-up one,
// so a floor-at-a-wall-foot whose hemisphere is half bricked up still averaged
// ABOVE the straight-up threshold and read as fully open: the +17-point corner
// over-brightening the first build record fenced.
//
// THE TEST, now. Two things follow from the atlas being a moment pair:
//
//   1. The threshold must be the INTEGRATED escape distance — what the texel
//      would hold if every ray in its lobe escaped: E_int(d) = 1.414213562 *
//      dot( A(d), numProbes ), where A_i(d) is the cosine-lobe mean of |w_i|
//      around d. Computed exactly for the 12x12 octahedral grid with upstream's
//      own weights (corner directions for the weights, texel centres for the
//      rays, exactly as the C++ does it) it is well fitted per axis by
//      A_i(d) = 0.396 + 0.275 * d_i^2 (aligned 0.67, transverse 0.40 — the
//      continuous values are 2/3 and 4/(3 pi); the fit's worst error over all
//      144 texels is 5% absolute). The script that derived it is recorded in
//      the lane report; kIfdDepthRes = 12 is the constant it stands on.
//
//   2. Given a mean and a mean-square, the escape FRACTION is a two-point
//      mixture problem — rays that escaped (at E_int) and rays that hit (at
//      something shorter) — and its closed form is the DDGI paper's own
//      Chebyshev visibility test evaluated at the escape distance:
//          f = var / ( (E - mean)^2 + var ),   var = meanSq - mean^2
//      (1 when mean >= E). Sanity: all rays hit at one distance -> var 0 ->
//      f 0 (the sealed room); half escape, half hit near -> f 1/2; all escape
//      -> 1. Real hit distances spread, which leaves a sealed room a small
//      residual f (measured 0.17 at the worst pixel of gi.ddgi_ambient's
//      room), so a knee below which f is ZERO keeps the sealed-room invariance
//      exact rather than merely small — the constants are just below.
//
// TAPS: ONE, along the field-space normal, and that is a measured decision
// (build record, rayon2 S1). The atlas already integrates the pixel's cosine
// hemisphere, so a tap tilted away from the normal has a lobe that dips below
// the surface's own horizon and reads its own floor as occlusion: upstream's
// 6-cone diffuse set on a tangent frame around the normal (the machinery is
// kept below, the count is a literal in the foreach) darkened OPEN floor to
// 53% of the cone reference against 85% for the single tap, and bought no
// corner shape for it (-3.5 against -6.6 points from the reference, both
// inside the gate). Over a pre-integrated atlas, more taps is a double blur.
//
// WHAT IT IS NOT. Still a proxy: the mixture model is exact only for
// two-valued distributions, the threshold is a fit, and the depth atlas is
// bilinear over 12x12 texels. It is gated on `ambient_sh` — the only ambient
// mode this engine ever sets (OgreEngine::ensureHlms forces HlmsPbs::AmbientSh),
// so the hemisphere and fixed branches of DoAmbientLighting are unreachable
// here and deliberately not reproduced; an engine that stopped forcing
// AmbientSh would silently lose this term rather than get a wrong one. The
// MONOCHROME SH variant is excluded for the same reason and one more: its
// irradianceSH returns a scalar, so the term would not even compile there.
//
// THE DIAL is `GiParams::ddgiAmbient`, riding jahIfd.y beside the intensity, and
// 0 turns the whole term off through a UNIFORM branch — so "DDGI without the
// fix" is not a rebuild, it is a const-buffer write, which is what lets the
// suite A/B it and what makes the sealed-room invariance assertion meaningful.
// jahIfd.zw carry the field's Y and Z probe counts, which upstream's own render
// params do NOT contain (only Nx and Nx*Ny reach the shader,
// OgreIrradianceField.cpp:812-813) and the threshold above needs all three.
//
// SCOPE: the whole file is gated on the `irradiance_field` property, which
// HlmsPbs sets only while a field is bound. With no field bound (every scene
// that has not opted in, which in P1 is all of them by default) not one line of
// this file reaches the generated shader, and undefining a piece that was never
// defined is a no-op.

@property( irradiance_field )

@undefpiece( applyIrradianceField )
@piece( applyIrradianceField )

	// ifdGridPos in range [0; mNumProbes)
	float3 ifdGridPos =
		transformPos3( inPs.pos.xyz, //
					   passBuf.irradianceField.viewToIrradianceFieldRow0,
					   passBuf.irradianceField.viewToIrradianceFieldRow1,
					   passBuf.irradianceField.viewToIrradianceFieldRow2 );

	float3 ifdGridProbeOrigin = trunc( ifdGridPos );
	float3 ifdSpaceNormal = normalize( transformDir3( pixelData.normal, //
									   passBuf.irradianceField.viewToIrradianceFieldRow0,
									   passBuf.irradianceField.viewToIrradianceFieldRow1,
									   passBuf.irradianceField.viewToIrradianceFieldRow2 ) );

	// ifdAlpha is how far from the floor( ifdGridPos ). on [0, 1] for each axis.
	float3 ifdAlpha = saturate( fract( ifdGridPos ) );

	float3 ifdIrradiance = float3( 0, 0, 0 );
	float sumIfdWeight = 0;
@property( ambient_sh && !ambient_sh_monochrome && vct_num_probes )
	// OURS: the cage-weighted sky visibility, and everything the taps need
	// that does not change per probe. A tangent frame around the field-space
	// normal (the axis least aligned with it seeds the cross product), the
	// three probe counts the threshold needs (upstream's render params carry
	// only Nx and Nx*Ny; Y and Z ride jahIfd.zw), and the tap set.
	float ifdSkyVis = 0;
	float3 ifdVisT = abs( ifdSpaceNormal.x ) < 0.9 ? float3( 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 ) : float3( 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 );
	ifdVisT = normalize( cross( ifdVisT, ifdSpaceNormal ) );
	float3 ifdVisB = cross( ifdSpaceNormal, ifdVisT );
	float3 ifdNumProbes = float3( passBuf.irradianceField.numProbesAggregated.x,
								  passBuf.jahIfd.z, passBuf.jahIfd.w );
	// CALIBRATION, two constants, both measured (build record, rayon2 S1):
	// ifdVisEscapeScale scales the integrated escape distance so that OPEN
	// FLOOR reads 1 -- the rays whose cone footprint grazes the floor exit the
	// march early, and they are the near-horizontal ones carrying the largest
	// escape distances, so the integrated mean of a fully open lobe sits a
	// little below the all-escaped value. ifdVisKnee: a Chebyshev escape
	// fraction at or below it is ZERO (a short smoothstep ramp above it, no
	// re-stretch), which is what keeps a sealed room bit-identical with the
	// term on: the room's residual (hit distances spread, so var > 0) measured
	// under the knee with margin.
	const float ifdVisEscapeScale = 0.9;
	const float ifdVisKnee = 0.3;
	const float ifdVisKneeRamp = 0.1;
	float3 ifdVisDirs[6] =
		OGRE_ARRAY_START( float3 )
			float3( 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 ),
			float3( 0.866025, 0.0, 0.5 ),
			float3( 0.267617, 0.823639, 0.5 ),
			float3( -0.700629, 0.509037, 0.5 ),
			float3( -0.700629, -0.509037, 0.5 ),
			float3( 0.267617, -0.823639, 0.5 )
		OGRE_ARRAY_END;
	// Weights for the tap count in use (1): the centre tap alone. The 6-tap
	// set is 0.25, 0.15, 0.15, 0.15, 0.15, 0.15.
	float ifdVisWeights[6] = OGRE_ARRAY_START( float ) 1.0, 0.15, 0.15, 0.15, 0.15, 0.15 OGRE_ARRAY_END;
@end

	// Iterate over adjacent probe cage
	for( int i = 0; i < 8; ++i )
	{
		// Compute the offset grid coord and clamp to the probe grid boundary
		// Offset = 0 or 1 along each axis
		float3 probeOffset = float3( int3( i, i >> 1, i >> 2 ) & int3( 1, 1, 1 ) );
		float3 probeOrigin = ifdGridProbeOrigin + probeOffset;

		IrfProbeIndex probeIdx =
			getProbeIdx( probeOrigin, passBuf.irradianceField.numProbesAggregated.xy );

		float3 dir = probeOrigin - ifdGridPos;
		float r = length( dir );
		dir *= 1.0 / r;

		// Ignore probes that are behind us, but don't black them out completely
		// as detailed surface may otherwise have very few probes ppointing at it
		float weight;
		weight = dot( dir, ifdSpaceNormal ) * 200.0;
		weight = saturate( weight ) + 0.2;

		// Compute the trilinear weights based on the grid cell vertex to smoothly
		// transition between probes. Avoid ever going entirely to zero because that
		// will cause problems at the border probes.
		// We're using 1-a when offset = 0 and a when offset = 1.
		float3 trilinear;
		trilinear.x = probeOffset.x < 1 ? ( 1.0 - ifdAlpha.x ) : ifdAlpha.x;
		trilinear.y = probeOffset.y < 1 ? ( 1.0 - ifdAlpha.y ) : ifdAlpha.y;
		trilinear.z = probeOffset.z < 1 ? ( 1.0 - ifdAlpha.z ) : ifdAlpha.z;

		// Visibility (Chebyshev)
		float2 ifdDepthUV = getIrradianceFieldXY(
			-dir, probeIdx, passBuf.irradianceField.depthBorderedRes,
			passBuf.irradianceField.depthFullWidth, passBuf.irradianceField.depthInvFullResolution );
		float2 temp = OGRE_SampleLevel( ifdDepth, ifdSampler, ifdDepthUV, 0 ).xy;
		float mean = temp.x;
		float meanSq = temp.y;
		if( r > mean )
		{
			float variance = abs( mean * mean - meanSq ) + 1e-6;
			float dev = ( r - mean );
			float chebyshevWeight = variance / ( variance + dev * dev );
			chebyshevWeight = max( chebyshevWeight * chebyshevWeight * chebyshevWeight, 0.0 );

			weight *= chebyshevWeight;
		}

		// Avoid zero weight
		weight = max( 0.000001, weight );

		const float crushThreshold = 0.2;
		if (weight < crushThreshold) {
			weight *= weight * weight * (1.0 / (crushThreshold*crushThreshold));
		}

		weight *= trilinear.x * trilinear.y * trilinear.z;

		float2 ifdColourUV = getIrradianceFieldXY(
			ifdSpaceNormal, probeIdx, passBuf.irradianceField.irradBorderedRes,
			passBuf.irradianceField.irradFullWidth, passBuf.irradianceField.irradInvFullResolution );

		float3 irrColour = OGRE_SampleLevel( ifdColour, ifdSampler, ifdColourUV, 0 ).xyz;
		ifdIrradiance += irrColour * weight;
		sumIfdWeight += weight;

@property( ambient_sh && !ambient_sh_monochrome && vct_num_probes )
		// OURS: the sky-visibility taps for this cage probe. The branch is
		// UNIFORM (jahIfd.y is a pass constant), so with the dial at 0 not one
		// instruction of this executes and the frame is bit-identical to a
		// build without the term.
		if( passBuf.jahIfd.y > 0.0 )
		{
			float ifdProbeVis = 0.0;
			@foreach( 1, t )
			{
				float3 ifdTapDir = ifdVisT * ifdVisDirs[@t].x + ifdVisB * ifdVisDirs[@t].y +
								   ifdSpaceNormal * ifdVisDirs[@t].z;
				float2 ifdVisUV = getIrradianceFieldXY(
					ifdTapDir, probeIdx, passBuf.irradianceField.depthBorderedRes,
					passBuf.irradianceField.depthFullWidth,
					passBuf.irradianceField.depthInvFullResolution );
				float2 ifdVisMoments = OGRE_SampleLevel( ifdDepth, ifdSampler, ifdVisUV, 0 ).xy;
				// The integrated escape distance for this tap's lobe (header,
				// item 1), then the Chebyshev test at it (item 2).
				float3 ifdVisA = float3( 0.396, 0.396, 0.396 ) + 0.275 * ifdTapDir * ifdTapDir;
				// THE SOURCE DECIDES THE UNIT (rayon2 S3). A voxel-fed probe stores a
				// miss at the march limit, 1.414 x dot( |dir|, numProbes ); a
				// raster-fed probe (IrradianceFieldRaster, CubemapToIfd) stores it
				// at the capture camera's FAR plane x dot( |dir|, probes per unit ),
				// so the host sends far x scale x probesPerUnit on jahIfd2.xyz. The
				// branch is UNIFORM (jahIfd2.w is a pass constant) and the voxel
				// expression is untouched, which is what keeps voxel-fed frames
				// byte-identical.
				float ifdVisEscape = passBuf.jahIfd2.w > 0.5 ?
									 dot( ifdVisA, passBuf.jahIfd2.xyz ) :
									 1.414213562 * ifdVisEscapeScale * dot( ifdVisA, ifdNumProbes );
				float ifdVisU = ifdVisMoments.x / ifdVisEscape;
				float ifdVisV = ifdVisMoments.y / ( ifdVisEscape * ifdVisEscape );
				float ifdVisVar = max( ifdVisV - ifdVisU * ifdVisU, 0.0 );
				float ifdVisMiss = 1.0 - ifdVisU;
				float ifdVisF = ifdVisMiss <= 0.0 ? 1.0 :
								ifdVisVar / ( ifdVisMiss * ifdVisMiss + ifdVisVar + 1e-8 );
				ifdVisF *= smoothstep( ifdVisKnee, ifdVisKnee + ifdVisKneeRamp, ifdVisF );
				ifdProbeVis += ifdVisWeights[@t] * ifdVisF;
			}
			@end
			ifdSkyVis += weight * ifdProbeVis;
		}
@end
	}

	// THE FIRST LINE THAT IS NOT UPSTREAM'S. Upstream writes
	//     pixelData.envColourD.xyz += ifdIrradiance * ( 1.0 / sumIfdWeight );
	// and we scale that by jahIfd.x, the DDGI diffuse intensity the host writes
	// into the pass buffer (JahshakaEngine's FogHlmsListener; the default is
	// calibrated against the pre-DDGI VCT diffuse, GiParams::ddgiIntensity).
	// 1.0 reproduces upstream exactly.
	pixelData.envColourD.xyz += ifdIrradiance * ( passBuf.jahIfd.x / sumIfdWeight );

@property( ambient_sh && !ambient_sh_monochrome && vct_num_probes )
	// AND THE AMBIENT THE VOLUME SWALLOWED, times the sky visibility above.
	// envColourD ONLY: the VCT specular path still adds its own ambient to
	// envColourS (Vct_piece_ps.any's specular branch), and touching that would
	// count it twice. The world-space normal transform is the one
	// DoAmbientLighting uses (AmbientLighting_piece_ps.any:66-67) — the
	// left-handed cubemap frame with X flipped — because irradianceSH's
	// coefficients are stored in that frame.
	if( passBuf.jahIfd.y > 0.0 )
	{
		float3 ifdWsNormal = mul( passBuf.invViewMatCubemap, pixelData.normal );
		ifdWsNormal.x = -ifdWsNormal.x;
		pixelData.envColourD.xyz += irradianceSH( ifdWsNormal PASSBUF_ARG ) *
									( passBuf.jahIfd.y * ifdSkyVis / sumIfdWeight );
	}
@end
@end

@end
